media: iris: backport upstream 7.3 driver with SC7280/Gen2 support

Replace the 6.18-era iris (decode-only, no kodiak support) with the
driver from linux @ 66498c75b4f8 (7.3-rc1, 2026-08-24). Adds SC7280
platform data, HFI Gen2 protocol support, and Gen2 firmware autodetect
(vpu20_p1_gen2_s6.mbn via QC_IMAGE_VERSION_STRING scan, Gen1 fallback),
plus the GDSC HW-mode-after-boot fix.

6.18 compatibility shims included:
- iris_618_compat.h (force-included via ccflags-y): kzalloc_obj,
  V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1, qcom_ubwc_* accessors on the vendor ubwc struct
- iris_probe.c: 6.18 genpd has const num_pd_names; build the SM8250
  fallback attach-data with a designated initializer instead of
  decrementing the member
- Kconfig: drop "select QCOM_PAS" (no such symbol in 6.18; PAS ops are
  shimmed onto qcom_scm, see patch 0002)

Verified: compiles clean as a module against radxa/kernel 559f4f92
(6.18.2) with aarch64-nerves-linux-gnu-gcc 15.3.0.

